### 🟠 Major (strongly recommended)
- `hooks/tests/contract-parity.test.sh:111-124` — The new JS-module check spawns `node -e '...'` with `require("./src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js")` — a **relative** require resolved against the child process's `process.cwd()`. Every other `node -e` invocation added to this same file passes the repo root explicitly (e.g. `validate-parity.js` receives `"$REPO_ROOT"` as `process.argv[2]` at line 15/80/91/129, or `hooks/tests/load-endpoints-env.test.sh:216` passes `process.argv[1]`). `lib.sh` (`hooks/tests/lib.sh:21-22`) never exports `REPO_ROOT` as an environment variable and this test file never `cd`s anywhere, so the require's success depends entirely on the *caller's* working directory at invocation time. `hooks/tests/run.sh:19` does `cd "$REPO_ROOT"` before running each `*.test.sh`, so the CI/umbrella path is safe — but the project's own doc (`hooks/tests/README.md:33`, "Single L2 file: `bash hooks/tests/state-checkpoint-empty-stdin.test.sh`") explicitly documents running an individual test file directly; if invoked from any cwd other than `REPO_ROOT` (e.g. `cd hooks/tests && bash contract-parity.test.sh`, a common IDE/terminal habit), the require throws `MODULE_NOT_FOUND`, `node -e` exits non-zero, and `assert_eq "$EXIT_AC_JS" "0" ...` (line 126) fails with a misleading "expected '0', got '1'" — a false test failure unrelated to the actual code under test. Fix: pass `$REPO_ROOT` into the script the same way the rest of the file does, e.g. `node -e 'const { resolveReviewLoopJson } = require(process.argv[1] + "/src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js"); ...' "$REPO_ROOT"` (single-quoted heredoc unchanged, just append the argv value), removing the cwd dependency.

